# Kibitz away from the end of the line plays a move at the cursor, as a board
# click and a pass do there — docs/game-modes.md use case 2 is exactly this
# workflow, and it says the engine will not *auto*-respond at a historical
# position, which is what asking once is for.
#
# It used to do nothing at all. `playKibitzMove()` hands the move to whoever is
# blocked in genmove and otherwise leaves it in `queuedMove` without waking
# anything — and while reviewing nobody is in genmove. Worse, the command called
# model.start() first, so a kibitz that did nothing still left the game Playing
# with the cursor mid-tree; the stale request then fired against a position
# nobody was looking at, and the turn order broke. From a recorded session.
#
#   ./tests/run_scenarios.sh tests/scenarios/kibitz_while_reviewing.scn

new_game 9
wait_idle
switch_player black human
switch_player white mock
wait_idle

click 2 2
click 2 2
wait_until move_count >= 2
click 4 4
click 4 4
wait_until move_count >= 4

# Back up two moves. The undone moves stay in the tree — undo is navigation, not
# deletion — so this is a review position with a continuation ahead of it.
undo move
wait_idle
undo move
wait_idle
expect view_position 2
expect at_end false
expect variations 1
expect phase paused
expect can_kibitz true

# One move, at the cursor, for whoever is to move there.
play once
wait_until move_count >= 3
expect view_position 3
expect at_end true

# And the game is still *not* running. Asking for one move while reviewing must
# not resume the match — that is what left the loop turning at a mid-tree cursor
# and broke the turn order afterwards. A click, by contrast, does resume it, and
# that difference is the documented one between asking once and handing every
# reply to the engine.
expect phase paused
expect thinking false

# It is the engine's turn now, so Start lights up — that is the affordance for
# resuming, and the reason kibitz does not resume by itself: asking for one move
# is not asking to restart the match you were reviewing.
expect can_start true

start
wait_until move_count >= 4
expect phase playing
expect color_to_move B
